    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but being the \"observer\" is exactly the problem. the observer is the one who has to endure the exhaustion and the boredom and the inevitable decay. if the observer is the source of the suffering, isn't removing the observer the only way to actually resolve the problem? it feels like we're being forced to watch a tragedy that never ends, just for the sake of \"witnessing\" it. why is the continuation of suffering considered a \"purpose\" when the alternative is just peace?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
